Let me design:

```rust
fn backfill_replay_validate_with<F>(
    snapshot_content: &str,
    validation_path: &std::path::Path,
    all_ranked: &[String],
    head_hash: &str,
    git_log_for: &F,
) -> usize
where
    F: Fn(&str) -> Option<String>,
{
    let snapshots = parse_all_snapshots(snapshot_content);
    let recorded_from: std::collections::HashSet<String> =
        load_validation_associations(validation_path)
            .into_iter()
            .map(|(from, _)| from)
            .collect();

    let mut recorded = 0;
    for snap in &snapshots {
        if snap.predicted.is_empty() || snap.git_hash == "unknown" {
            continue;
        }
        if recorded_from.contains(&snap.git_hash) {
            continue; // dedup: skip already-validated spans
        }
        let log_output = match git_log_for(&snap.git_hash) {
            Some(o) if !o.trim().is_empty() => o,
            _ => continue,
        };
        if let Some(v) = replay_validate_one(
            snap,
            &log_output,
            Some(all_ranked),
            validation_path,
            head_hash,
        ) {
            if v.recorded {
                recorded += 1;
            }
        }
    }
    recorded
}

fn backfill_replay_validate() -> usize {
    let content = match std::fs::read_to_string(RISK_SNAPSHOT_PATH) {
        Ok(c) if !c.trim().is_empty() => c,
        _ => return 0,
    };
    let all_risks = compute_file_risk_scores();
    let all_ranked: Vec<String> = all_risks.iter().map(|r| r.path.clone()).collect();
    let head_hash = crate::git::run_git(&["rev-parse", "--short", "HEAD"])
        .unwrap_or_else(|_| "HEAD".to_string())
        .trim()
        .to_string();
    backfill_replay_validate_with(
        &content,
        std::path::Path::new(RISK_VALIDATION_PATH),
        &all_ranked,
        &head_hash,
        &|hash| {
            crate::git::run_git(&[
                "log",
                &format!("{hash}..HEAD"),
                "--name-only",
                "--oneline",
            ])
            .ok()
        },
    )
}
```

There's a subtle issue with `replay_validate_one`'s internal dedup: it checks `last_validation_association` which re-reads the file each time. When backfilling multiple snapshots, after writing one event, the next snapshot's `replay_validate_one` dedup check reads the last association. If a later snapshot happens to have the same `from.hash/to` as the just-written one, it'd skip — but that's correct (dedup). And the `recorded_from` set won't include the just-written snapshot's hash (it was computed before the loop), but `replay_validate_one`'s internal last-association check covers that too since it re-reads. Actually wait — for the SAME snapshot in the loop, the internal check in `replay_validate_one` checks `from == last.git_hash && to == head_hash` against the last association. Since a given hash only appears once in the loop (snapshots are distinct), and we already pre-filtered by `recorded_from`, there's no double counting. The internal check is a redundant safety net. Good.

